  "description": "int lap_net_status(lap_net_status_t *out)  All calls return immediately. Six outbound IPv4 sockets per app (two on firmware before API 2.4). Join using LINK or the API 2.4 Wi-Fi service. Connect returns a handle >=0 or an error; poll state until CONNECTED or a negative error. Timeout (1..30000 ms) covers asynchronous DNS + connect, not stream lifetime. Host is DNS name or numeric IPv4, <=253 chars. IPv6/TLS/listening unsupported. send copies up to 4096 bytes into a bounded queue and returns bytes accepted (may be partial), EAGAIN if full/pending. Acceptance is not delivery. recv copies up to 4096 bytes, EAGAIN when empty/pending, 0 on peer EOF after queued bytes drain. Check negative errors; retry EAGAIN in later frames. Host strings and send/receive/status buffers are copied synchronously and may live on the callback stack. Close invalidates the handle immediately; worker releases it asynchronously. Closing the app closes every socket and discards queued bytes. Pointer contract: Synchronous input/output buffers may use the active callback stack; runtime retains no caller data buffer. Since API 1.3. Capability: none. Simulator: limited \u2014 Real nonblocking host IPv4 sockets and worker lifecycle; host DNS/Wi-Fi and wall-clock timing differ.",
  "scope": "c"
